{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.45-§7.3.46, step 7f. `scale-county`: Total Energy (91) for the gasoline passenger car at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, August 2020, weekday, hour 7, from the default database plus Washtenaw's COMPLETE county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county.esm`, built from moves.rs `setup-county.sql`). MOVESOutput is 729 rows: running exhaust (9101) on road types 1 to 5, 125 rows each, and start exhaust (9102) on road type 1, 104 rows. The RunSpec also names petroleum and fossil energy (92, 93) and well-to-pump (99), which are not MOVES5 pollutant-processes, and extended idle (9190), which a passenger car never emits.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the county database, against a twin. Every one of the 729 MOVESOutput rows equals the DEFAULT-domain `expand-roadtypes` snapshot's row at the same key (same county, year, month, hour and vehicle), and the two execution databases differ only in MOVES's SINGLE-scale REPLACE tables, which hold the 2020 rows the run reads, in `avft`, which leaves `sampleVehiclePopulation` the default's, and in the 9190 selection. So this run is `expand-roadtypes` with the county database's row merges in the path -- `zone` and `zoneRoadType` shadowing the default's rows with the default's own values -- and with a RunSpec that names road types 1 and 4 and gets all five, because ExecutionRunSpec selects every road type when road type 1 and running exhaust are both selected (\"Off-Network Idle requires all roadtypes\", conventions §100). `totalIdleFraction` is a whole-table copy in the county database (3,120 rows) and the three idle adjustment tables are empty there as in the default, so off-network idle reads the default's.\n\n729 of 729 with no model change beyond `expand-roadtypes`' -- the road type as an axis and off-network idle (PLAN.md §7.3.46) -- key set exact. `n_outputRate` is bound to 729, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/scale-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
